# Every line here is a regular expression, comments included, so no brackets.
# Keep everything configure stages or the compiler produces out of the R source
# tarball built by R CMD build. The package is source-distributed: configure
# fetches the C ABI at install time, or takes it from the INC and LIB dev
# override, so none of these belong in the distributable. There is no Windows
# build: risc0 has no Windows host and DESCRIPTION says OS_type unix.
^src/wickra_zk\.h$
^src/libwickra_zk\.(so|dylib|a)$
^src/wickra-zk-c\.tar\.gz$
^src/wickra-zk-c$
^src/Makevars$
^src/.*\.o$
^src/wickrazk\.(so|dylib)$
^src/symbols\.rds$
^\.gitignore$
# The cross-language golden parity test. It looks for golden/ in a parent
# directory, which exists in this repository and never in a built tarball, so
# `R CMD check` would run a test that silently skips its own subject. CI runs it
# directly from the repository instead; tests/smoke.R is what ships.
^tests/run_tests\.R$
